@doc """
A JSON value. It is one of six types: `Null`, `Bool`, `Number`,
`String`, `List<Value>`, or `Object`. A JSON array is a list of
values.

A literal builds a value in a position that expects one. A string or
boolean literal stays a `String` or a `Bool`, a number literal builds
a `Number`, a list literal builds a `List<Value>`, and a map literal
builds an `Object`. `JSON.NULL` is the null value.

Read a value with `match` and a typed binding for each type the
caller accepts.
"""
type Value = Null | Bool | Number | String | List<Value> | Object
